    <summary>Non-interactive SSH password authentication tool - native Win64 port</summary>
    <description>
sshpass is a utility designed for running SSH in non-interactive mode, providing the password via the command line, environment variable, or file.

This is a native Windows 64-bit port using the Windows ConPTY (Pseudo Console) API. No Cygwin or WSL required.

## Features
- Provide SSH password via command line (-p), file (-f), environment variable (-e), or stdin
- Detects host key warnings and returns appropriate exit codes
- Native Win64 binary - no Unix compatibility layer needed
- Requires Windows 10 version 1809 or later

## Usage
```
sshpass -p "password" ssh user@host
sshpass -f password.txt ssh user@host
sshpass -e ssh user@host
```
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/sharpninja/sshpass-win64/releases</releaseNotes>
